From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:38:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Shorten tWRRD between ranks

After a write to one rank the controller waits tWRRD_dr or tWRRD_dd
clocks before a read from another rank. refresh_timings() sets both to
the sum of the JEDEC times and nothing shortened them: on a ThinkPad
W541 with four dual-rank DIMMs they are 4, where mrc.bin ends at 3,
the only turnaround that differs between the two.

Add HASWELL_NRI_TURNAROUND: after the round trip step, run the
turnaround test of the REUT (PAT_WR_RD_TA, which setup_io_test() and
run_io_test() had and no step used) on all the ranks of each channel,
with the turnaround one clock shorter each time until it fails. The
result is the shortest value that passes plus one clock, and at most
one clock shorter than it was. It changes only if a value did fail:
the tests of the other steps work on one rank at a time, and a test
that passes down to one clock has not seen the turnaround either. Not
run in the training that is done again after a failure.

Not tried on a machine.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init.

Change-Id: I86146c42542f23117c07ade66ad2688afe54a0ed
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig         |  10 +
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/Makefile.mk  |   1 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c     |   1 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h   |   1 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/train_turnaround.c | 197 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 210 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_turnaround.c

